      "instance_name": "condescending_tone",
      "label": "Condescending Tone in Addressing Others",
      "description": "The phrase 'hello chocolate paradise princess' is a condescending and patronizing way to address someone, implying they are unworthy of serious consideration and are only valued for their indulgence or perceived femininity. This tone is often used to belittle or infantilize, especially when directed at women, and is a form of social dominance or power play.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_b4a00222"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0a4e6814",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "gendered_title_use",
      "label": "Use of Gendered Titles in Humor or Mockery",
      "description": "The meme relies on the use of a gendered title ('princess') to create humor or irony. This is a common trope in internet memes and comedy, where exaggerated or inappropriate titles are used to mock or highlight social norms. The title 'princess' is traditionally associated with femininity and is often used in a mocking or infantilizing way in modern contexts, especially when juxtaposed with a professional or serious setting like a kitchen.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_b4a00222"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
